WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.508
UUIDs generate 79

00:00:02.319 --> 00:00:03.439
times faster than

00:00:03.251 --> 00:00:03.982
ULIDs

00:00:04.518 --> 00:00:05.732
The author generated

00:00:05.579 --> 00:00:06.452
a million of

00:00:06.310 --> 00:00:07.230
each ID on

00:00:07.042 --> 00:00:07.654
Node .

00:00:07.466 --> 00:00:08.173
js

00:00:08.409 --> 00:00:09.871
UUID version 4

00:00:09.683 --> 00:00:10.815
hit about seven

00:00:10.627 --> 00:00:11.676
million a second

00:00:11.924 --> 00:00:13.326
ULID about 89

00:00:13.138 --> 00:00:13.916
thousand

00:00:14.446 --> 00:00:15.979
UUID version 4

00:00:15.790 --> 00:00:17.122
is sixteen random

00:00:16.934 --> 00:00:18.054
bytes with dashes

00:00:18.125 --> 00:00:19.457
while ULID packs

00:00:19.316 --> 00:00:20.884
a 48-bit timestamp

00:00:20.696 --> 00:00:21.285
first

00:00:21.333 --> 00:00:22.606
so only ULID

00:00:22.418 --> 00:00:23.573
sorts by creation

00:00:23.385 --> 00:00:23.950
time

00:00:24.470 --> 00:00:25.802
CUID2 runs a

00:00:25.614 --> 00:00:26.651
hash to resist

00:00:26.463 --> 00:00:27.076
guessing

00:00:27.218 --> 00:00:27.984
and the lesson

00:00:27.795 --> 00:00:28.526
is to pick

00:00:28.338 --> 00:00:29.234
for your database

00:00:29.045 --> 00:00:29.694
index

00:00:29.753 --> 00:00:30.755
not by habit

00:00:31.278 --> 00:00:32.292
Full story on

00:00:32.103 --> 00:00:32.999
the dashboard
